  "scenario": "Several siblings want a simple retro-game gift for their father and have found a PlayStation Classic bundle page, a generic 620-game plug-and-play page, and a preloaded RetroPie card page. They have also heard incompatible blanket claims: store popularity supposedly proves quality, while enthusiasts supposedly prove that every mini console has bad emulation lag and poor controllers. The frozen corpus instead contains sparse and non-comparable seller snapshots, model-specific evidence that PlayStation Classic and NES Classic implementations were received differently, general emulator and display-lag boundaries, and individual community preferences that cannot stand in for the father's game, controller, or latency tolerance. The research problem is to audit the three retail objects, separate emulator, display, controller, game, and preference questions, and produce a reversible recipient trial or defer decision without naming a universal mini-console winner.",
